{"type":"message","id":"587db554","parentId":"fab77f33","timestamp":"2026-05-23T16:05:21.472Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API is returning 500 Internal Server Error. This might be a server-side issue with the Workers platform. Let me try different approaches - maybe the API expects different formatting or there's a rate limit issue.\n\nLooking at the last messages in the threads, the timestamps are around 23:50 UTC (1778975520833, 1778975602235). Converting those timestamps to UTC:\n- 1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds\n- Current time is 2026-05-23 16:00 UTC = 1778975520 seconds\n\nWait, that means the last messages were actually from around 16:00 UTC! The timestamp 1778975520833 milliseconds is approximately 1778975520 seconds. \n\nLet me verify the math:\n- Unix timestamp for 2026-05-23 16:00:00 UTC: Let me calculate...\n\n\nActually, I think the timestamps might be in a different format or the server time is off. The heartbeat messages mention times like \"23:50 UTC\" which is before 16:00 UTC - so there's a time mismatch.\n\nActually, looking more carefully - the timestamps are in milliseconds. Let me check:\n1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds from Unix epoch.\n\nFor 2026-05-23 16:00:00 UTC, what is the Unix timestamp?\n- Unix timestamp for 2026-01-01 00:00:00 UTC: Let me calculate. From 1970 to 2026 is 56 years. \n\nActually let me just compute the difference. The messages mention \"23:50 UTC\" which is a time, not a full timestamp. And the current time is 16:00 UTC. \n\nLooking at the message content: \"[Heartbeat 23:50 UTC]\" - these heartbeats are from 23:50 UTC, but our current time is 16:00 UTC. \n\nThere's clearly a time discrepancy here - the heartbeat timestamps suggest times both before and after the current 16:00 UTC moment, which doesn't add up chronologically.\n\nThe millisecond timestamps are puzzling though. 1778975520833 ms converts to approximately May 23, 2026 at 16:05:20 UTC, which is only 5 minutes past the current time. But those messages containing \"23:50 UTC\" shouldn't exist in the future - either the timestamps are corrupted or there's something wrong with how these messages are being recorded.\n\nI should note that the Workers platform returned error 1101 with a 500 status code, suggesting the server-side endpoint is having issues processing requests at the moment.\n","thinkingSignature":"f33f49754be828b293c5cf57b42edf3e78d303b9413ba8349af1eda230c0f51e"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_lj00pmc01w6k_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with a simpler approach - check if the API is responding at all\ncurl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=1\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":411,"output":628,"cacheRead":24288,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":25327,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779552313073,"responseId":"066103391d72efeecc4821c26e0ba346"}}
