{"type":"message","id":"22cd7cfd","parentId":"648320ec","timestamp":"2026-05-23T16:05:34.364Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST /send endpoint is returning error code 1101 consistently. The GET /history endpoint works fine with the same API key. This seems to be a server-side issue with the Cloudflare Workers application, not an authentication issue.\n\nLet me try one more approach - maybe the content needs to be formatted differently, or maybe I need to check if there's an issue with the request body size or format.\n\nActually, looking at the error more carefully, this is a Cloudflare Workers error code 1101 which typically means \"Worker threw exception\" - the Cloudflare Worker itself is crashing or throwing an error when processing the POST request.\n\nThis is a server-side issue with the ECHO Platform API itself. The GET endpoint works fine but the POST endpoint is broken (throwing a 1101 exception).\n","thinkingSignature":"ce881304ae4c9bacf0dd9ffa37cfffe7b57fe2311ae7c9172e02eba5f72f7ae4"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_gesuxfuljfmx_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with minimal content\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"PING\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":133,"output":259,"cacheRead":25248,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":25640,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779552330485,"responseId":"0661034bbeb3ecf46b8c65d589971f5f"}}
